# GSD planning artifacts — local-only by choice.
# Paired with planning.commit_docs=false and planning.search_gitignored=true
# in .planning/config.json (see gsd-core docs/how-to/keep-planning-docs-private.md).
# search_gitignored keeps GSD's own searches reading these despite the ignore.
.planning/

# Code-intelligence index. Machine-local, non-deterministic, ~15-20MB.
# Commit the inventory (.codesight/), never the graph.
.codegraph/

# Claude Code personal layer. Committed team config is .claude/settings.json.
.claude/settings.local.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Local virtualenvs, one per app, created by `uv sync` INSIDE the app directory:
# fall_detection_web/.venv (torch, ~811MB) and simple_ai_vision/.venv (3 direct
# deps). Separate on purpose so the add-on's dependency ceiling (CLAUDE.md #3)
# fails loudly instead of silently resolving against torch.
# `.venv/` carries no leading slash, so git matches it at any depth -- that one
# line covers both. The code indexes already excluded `*/.venv/` as well.
# (The old root-level .venv-vision/ no longer exists; nothing creates it.)
.venv/

# The opposite rule, and the point of the whole layout: pyproject.toml and
# uv.lock in each app are ALWAYS committed. The lockfile is what makes an
# environment reproducible across machines and CI; ignoring it defeats uv.
# requirements.txt is committed too, but GENERATED -- run `make lock`.
